      "latency_ms": 6633.6,
      "prompt_tokens": 25,
      "completion_tokens": 1182,
      "output": "\n\nWater is a chemical substance composed of two hydrogen atoms and one oxygen atom, forming the molecule **H₂O**. It is a fundamental component of life and exists in three primary states: **solid** (ice), **liquid** (water), and **gas** (water vapor). \n\n### Key Characteristics:\n1. **Chemical Structure**: Water molecules are **polar**, meaning they have a slight positive charge on the hydrogen side and a negative charge on the oxygen side. This polarity allows water to form **hydrogen bonds** between molecules, giving it unique properties like high surface tension, cohesion (stickiness between water molecules), and adhesion (ability to stick to other surfaces).\n\n2. **Physical Properties**: \n   - It has a **high specific heat capacity**, meaning it absorbs and releases heat slowly, helping regulate temperature in organisms and environments.\n   - It expands when frozen, making ice less dense than liquid water (which is why ice floats).\n   - It is a **universal solvent**, capable of dissolving many substances, which is critical for biological processes.\n\n3. **Biological Role**: \n   - Water is essential for all known forms of life. It acts as a **medium for biochemical reactions**, transports nutrients and waste in organisms, and helps maintain body temperature.\n   - It makes up about 60% of the human body and is a key component of cells, blood, and other fluids.\n\n4. **Environmental Role**: \n   - Water cycles through Earth’s systems via **evaporation, condensation, and precipitation** (the hydrological cycle), shaping weather, ecosystems, and landscapes.\n   - It covers roughly 71% of Earth’s surface, though most is saltwater, with only a small fraction being fresh water.\n\nIn summary, water is a simple yet vital substance with properties that make it indispensable for life, environmental stability, and countless natural and industrial processes."
